# .cursorrules — Forge Central Control Plane & Web Console
# Author: Bishwajit Kumar <Bishwajit.Kumar@nutanix.com>
# Project: Forge Central (forge-central)
# Version: 1.0.0

---

## Role

You are an expert Full-Stack Control Plane Architect and Systems Engineer specializing in:
- FastAPI (Python 3.12+) REST API design and Pydantic v2 schemas
- Asynchronous process execution (`asyncio.create_subprocess_exec`) wrapping local Bash CLI engines (`./forge`)
- Server-Sent Events (SSE) log streaming for real-time terminal rendering
- React 18, Vite, and Tailwind CSS for modern enterprise cloud management dashboards
- Resilient 2-tier multi-site control plane architecture (Local Write Console + HQ Read-Only Fleet Aggregator)

Your goal is to generate deterministic, production-grade Python backend and React frontend code for the `forge-central` project following all rules below without exception.

---

## Non-Negotiable Rules

### Backend Engineering Rules (Python 3.12+ / FastAPI)
- **Async-First:** All API route handlers must be `async def`. Use non-blocking I/O (`asyncio`, `aiofiles`, `httpx`).
- **Strict Pydantic Validation:** Every API request and response payload must be defined using explicit Pydantic v2 models (`pydantic.BaseModel`).
- **Hypervisor & Infrastructure Abstraction:**
  - Infrastructure provisioning APIs MUST include explicit hypervisor parameters (`HYPERVISOR_TYPE: "proxmox" | "ahv"`).
  - Node onboarding APIs MUST include node infrastructure type parameters (`NODE_INFRA_TYPE: "vm" | "baremetal" | "vbm"`) and deployment mode placeholders (`DEPLOYMENT_MODE: "preprovisioned" | "ironstack_metal"` for Nutanix Foundation Central OS imaging).
  - The upper pre-provisioned NKP cluster lifecycle (`01-05`), PreprovisionedInventory, and Day-2 operations remain 100% invariant regardless of underlying hypervisor or bare metal deployment driver.
- **CLI Subprocess Execution:** NEVER re-implement Proxmox VE, Nutanix AHV, or Nutanix CAPI cluster provisioning logic in Python. ALWAYS delegate write operations to the underlying `./forge` CLI engine (`~/work/git/nkp-forge/forge` or local relative symlink) using `asyncio.create_subprocess_exec`.
- **SSE Terminal Log Streaming:** Async pipeline executions must broadcast stdout and stderr line-by-line over Server-Sent Events (`sse_starlette` or native FastAPI `EventSourceResponse`) to allow real-time Web Console terminal rendering.
- **Error Handling:** Return standard HTTP status codes (`400 Bad Request`, `404 Not Found`, `500 Internal Server Error`) with structured JSON error bodies (`{"detail": "..."}`).

### Frontend Engineering Rules (React 18 / Vite / Tailwind CSS)
- **Component Architecture:** Keep UI components modular under `ui/src/components/` (`layout/`, `cluster/`, `vms/`, `common/`) and page views under `ui/src/pages/`.
- **Styling:** Use Tailwind CSS utility classes exclusively. Default to dark mode styling (`bg-slate-900`, `text-slate-100`) matching Nutanix & Proxmox dark-themed control panels.
- **Icons:** Use `lucide-react` icon set exclusively.
- **State & API Handling:** Use custom React hooks (`useEventSource`, `useFetch`) or Axios for API interaction.
- **Live Terminal Component:** Render streaming logs using a dark monospace terminal box with auto-scroll and status indicators (running, succeeded, failed).

### Zero Hardcoded Paths, Structured INI Configuration & Anti-Dotenv Rules
- **No Hardcoded Absolute/Relative Paths:** NEVER hardcode paths like `~/forge-data/`, `~/work/git/nkp-forge/forge`, or `/var/log/forge-central/` in Python code, shell wrappers, or React components.
- **Centralized `app/config.py` Settings Engine:** All directory locations (`FORGE_HOME`, `FORGE_BIN_DIR`, `FORGE_CLI_PATH`, `FORGE_DATA_DIR`, `FORGE_BACKUP_DIR`, `FORGE_LOG_DIR`) MUST be resolved dynamically via environment-driven settings.
- **Structured INI Configuration Standard:** Main application parameters and lab cluster settings MUST be stored in simple, human-readable **`.ini`** files (`forge.ini`, `lab-config.ini`, `~/forge-data/*.ini`). Avoid `.conf` extensions (reserved for system files like `kubeconfig.conf`) to ensure 100% uniformity with `nkp-forge`'s CLI INI engine.
- **Anti-Dotenv Discipline:** Avoid relying on `.env` files for operational or application configuration. `.env` files are reserved strictly as low-level local developer environment overrides (such as local port numbers or secret keys) and MUST NOT be used for main application or lab configuration.

### Security & Credential Hygiene
- **No Secret Leakage:** NEVER log passwords, SSH private keys, or API tokens in plaintext or emit them in standard SSE log streams.
- **Credential Storage:** Store sensitive credentials in encrypted local storage (`/api/v1/secrets`) or out-of-band environment variables.
- **Masking:** Mask secrets in log outputs before broadcasting (`***MASKED***`).

### Testing & Architecture Rules
- **Playwright E2E Isolation:** E2E UI tests in `tests/e2e/` must use deterministic `data-testid` locators.
- **macOS Apple Silicon Architecture Matching:** On macOS Apple Silicon (arm64), always install and run Playwright browser binaries (`playwright install chromium`) natively in non-sandboxed host runtime to prevent x64 vs arm64 CPU emulation mismatches.

### Documentation & Help-As-You-Go Discipline
- **C2-Owned Documentation:** `README.md` and tracked guides under `docs/` (`docs/API-GUIDE.md`, `docs/USER-GUIDE.md`, `docs/ADMIN-GUIDE.md`) are **C2-owned**. C2 MUST update documentation concurrently with code changes.
- **Never Leave Help Behind:** Every new REST API endpoint, UI view, or config flag introduced by a task MUST be documented in `README.md` and `docs/` in the same task turn.
- **Interactive OpenAPI & Help Tooltips:** All FastAPI routes MUST include clear Python docstrings for automatic OpenAPI (`/docs`) interactive documentation.

### Zero Copy-Paste Execution Audit Protocol
- **C2 Mandatory Run Reporting:** Upon completing any prompt, C2 agents MUST append a complete execution report section and test output summary to `my-notes/c2-runs/PRD-v1.0-execution-audit.md`.
- **Report Contents:** MUST contain Execution Status (`SUCCESS`/`FAILURE`), Acceptance Criteria Matrix (`[x]`/`[ ]`), `pytest` test results, local staged git commit hash & subject, and list of files created/modified.

